 :cli/usage "cljpass - team password manager with per-entry permissions

Users:
  cljpass                                  start the desktop app
  cljpass gui [--idle SECONDS]
  cljpass enroll --server URL --org-hash H [--user NAME] [--kerberos]
  cljpass open FILE [--new] [--keyfile K]  local mode with a KeePass file (no server)
  cljpass connect [--server URL --org-hash H] local file -> server (run again after approval)
  cljpass disconnect FILE [--keyfile K] [--force]  server -> local file
  cljpass status | sync | list | fingerprint
  cljpass export-device --out FILE         identity for a new device (with one-time code)
  cljpass import-device FILE [--server URL --org-hash H]
  cljpass kdbx-import FILE [--keyfile K]   take over a KeePass database (lossless)
  cljpass kdbx-export FILE [--keyfile K]   all readable entries as a KeePass file
  cljpass kdbx-sync FILE [--keyfile K]     local: synchronize with another KeePass file (like KeePass)
  cljpass rotate [ID|TITLE ...] [--probe] [--no-probe] [--code 123456]
                                           change the password at the target, then in the vault (no name: what works here)
  cljpass agent ...                        access for an LLM session without passwords (cljpass agent help)
  cljpass import FILE [--format kdbx|xml|csv] [--keyfile K]
                                             KeePass XML, CSV (KeePassXC, Bitwarden, browsers) or KDBX
  cljpass export FILE --format xml|csv|html|xsl [--xsl TEMPLATE] [--passwords]
                                             unencrypted: KeePass XML, CSV, HTML, XSL template

Server:
  cljpass server --db FILE [--port 8080] [--bind 0.0.0.0] [--init-token T]
                   [--keytab FILE --realm REALM [--principal HTTP/host@REALM] [--require-kerberos]]
                   [--trust-proxy]           client address from X-Forwarded-For (behind Caddy etc.)

Administration (with an admin identity):
  cljpass init --server URL --org NAME --init-token T [--user NAME] --recovery-out FILE
  cljpass requests                         open approval requests
  cljpass approve USER --fingerprint FP [--display-name NAME]
  cljpass disable USER
  cljpass group NAME [MEMBER ...]          set members (empty = remove all)
  cljpass ad-sync [--source adsi|FILE.json] [--prefix pw-]
  cljpass auto-approve [--watch SECONDS] [--ad-sync [--source ..] [--prefix ..]]
                                             approve requests confirmed by Kerberos (as a service with --watch)
  cljpass audit [--since SEQ] [--json]     server audit log, checks the hash chain
  cljpass recover USER --recovery-key FILE --out FILE
"
